{{- /*
  Per-entity canonical CRUD shape, parameterized over (Project, Domain, Entity).

  Emits:
    - gob registrations for the domain struct + input variants
    - the domain struct
    - CreationRequestInput, DatabaseCreationInput, UpdateRequestInput
    - <Entity>DataManager interface (CRUD core — Exists, Get, List,
      Create, Update, Archive). Bespoke methods (search indexing,
      custom state transitions, etc.) are intentionally out of scope
      for the schema-driven path and must be added by hand if needed.
    - Update method, merging UpdateRequestInput into the receiver
    - ValidateWithContext for each input variant
    - Convert<Entity>ToDatabaseCreationInput — scalar-to-scalar mapping

  Routing decisions:
    - belongs_to / belongs_to_account / belongs_to_user / created_by_user
      are *server-supplied* (URL nest, session). They appear on the
      domain struct and DatabaseCreationInput, never on
      CreationRequestInput.
    - links_to FKs are *client-supplied* and flow through both inputs.

  DataManager signature conventions (see funcmap helpers existsArgNames /
  listArgNames / archiveArgNames):
    - Exists / Get: (parent-chain-ids..., selfID) — outermost-parent-first,
      self last.
    - List Get<Plural>: takes parent-chain-ids (for nested entities) or
      a single scope arg (accountID / userID) for top-level entities.
    - Archive: parent-chain-ids..., selfID for nested entities;
      (selfID, accountID|userID) for top-level entities that carry
      scope; (selfID) for globally-scoped top-level entities.

  These conventions are consistent but differ from a handful of upstream
  entities that chose bespoke orderings (e.g., MealListItem). Accepted
  drift — see parity_checklist.md.

  Output is gofmt'd by the renderer (PlannedFile.IsGo=true), so loose
  whitespace here is fine.
*/ -}}
